In a prior conversation, James sought help with an automated Bash script meant to run daily on his Mac at 2pm. He encountered an error indicating that `Rscript` could not be spawned, despite it being present on his system. I identified that the issue likely stemmed from differences in the execution environment's `PATH`. I suggested specifying the full path to `Rscript` in his Julia script, verifying permissions for `eval.R`, and considering the automation method (e.g., `launchd` or cron jobs) to ensure proper environment settings. James was encouraged to provide further details about how the script is executed for more tailored assistance.
